  "notes": "Boot a Harlem Globetrotters On Tour ROM from empty NVRAM with the ball in the outhole (public 8 closed) and PinMAME's built-in mechanisms disabled; the scenario names no game. Coin up, start a game (the press must change public 19, the flipper-enable relay), and let the ball leave the outhole. Then close the drop-target switches 1, 3 and 4, holding each, and only then close public 2, the address the legacy platform file calls Ball Roll Tilt and the game file Drop Target 2. The score displays and lamps record what the ROM does with each closure, and public 19 shows whether it tilts. Drain the ball and require the ball release (7) to serve ball 2.",
